## GitHub Workflow

### Branch Strategy

```
main        ← Production releases only (protected)
  ↑
develop     ← Integration branch (default, protected)
  ↑
feature/*   ← Feature branches
fix/*       ← Bug fixes
```

### Branch Protection

Both `main` and `develop` are protected:
- Requires 1 approval before merge
- Stale approvals dismissed on new commits
- No force pushes
- No deletions

### Feature Development Workflow

**1. Create GitHub Issue first:**
```bash
# Create a feature issue
gh issue create --title "feat(stamps): add geofence validation" \
  --body "## Description
Add 50m geofence check for stamp collection.

## Tasks
- [ ] Add distance calculation helper
- [ ] Validate location in collect endpoint
- [ ] Return appropriate error if out of range" \
  --label "enhancement"

# Create a bug fix issue
gh issue create --title "fix(auth): handle expired OTP" \
  --body "OTP verification fails silently when expired." \
  --label "bug"
```

**2. Create branch from issue:**
```bash
# This creates a branch linked to the issue
gh issue develop <issue-number> --checkout

# Branch name auto-generated: <issue-number>-feat-stamps-add-geofence-validation
```

**3. Make changes & commit:**
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "feat(stamps): add geofence validation"
```

**4. Push & create PR:**
```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base develop --title "feat(stamps): add geofence validation" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- Added 50m geofence validation for stamp collection

## Changes
- Added `calculateDistance()` helper using Haversine formula
- Validate user location in `/stamps/collect` endpoint

Fixes #<issue-number>

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
EOF
)"
```

**5. After approval, merge to develop**

**6. Release to production:**
```bash
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git merge develop
git push origin main
```

### Issue Labels

| Label | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `enhancement` | New feature |
| `bug` | Bug fix |
| `documentation` | Docs only |
| `backend` | Backend changes |
| `flutter` | Flutter app changes |
| `priority:high` | Urgent |

### Commit Message Convention

```
type(scope): description

Types: feat, fix, docs, refactor, test, chore
Scope: auth, stamps, rewards, merchant, user, backend, core
```

Examples:
- `feat(stamps): add geofence validation`
- `fix(auth): handle expired OTP`
- `docs: update API reference`

### Quick Reference

```bash
# Create issue
gh issue create --title "type(scope): description" --label "enhancement"

# Create branch from issue (auto-links in GitHub)
gh issue develop <N> --checkout

# View issue
gh issue view <N>

# Create PR that closes issue
gh pr create --base develop --body "Fixes #N"
```

